(>> 4.4 The 7-Layer OSI Reference Model \(ISO 7498\)) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Theoretical standard model partitioning network communications into 7 hierarchical) Tj
T*
(abstraction layers:) Tj
T*
(* Layer 7 - Application: User interface, network services \(HTTP, DNS, SMTP, FTP\).) Tj
T*
(* Layer 6 - Presentation: Syntax translation, character encoding, data compression,) Tj
T*
(encryption/decryption \(SSL/TLS\).) Tj
T*
(* Layer 5 - Session: Dialog establishment, checkpointing, token management, session) Tj
T*
(synchronization.) Tj
T*
(* Layer 4 - Transport: End-to-end reliable process-to-process delivery, segmentation,) Tj
T*
(flow control, port addressing \(TCP, UDP\). Data unit: Segment / Datagram.) Tj
T*
(* Layer 3 - Network: Host-to-host delivery, logical addressing \(IP\), path) Tj
T*
(determination, routing. Data unit: Packet.) Tj
T*
(* Layer 2 - Data Link: Hop-to-hop node delivery, physical MAC addressing, framing,) Tj
T*
(error detection \(CRC\), flow control, channel access \(CSMA/CD\). Data unit: Frame.) Tj
T*
(* Layer 1 - Physical: Transmission of raw unstructured bit streams over physical) Tj
T*
(medium, voltage levels, signaling rates, cable connectors. Data unit: Bit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
