([PROBLEM 1: Mesh vs Star Topology Enterprise Scalability Calculation]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Statement: An enterprise connects 16 servers in a mission-critical datacenter.) Tj
T*
(Calculate and compare: \(1\) Total dedicated communication links required for a fully) Tj
T*
(connected Mesh topology vs a Star topology, and \(2\) Total hardware I/O ports required) Tj
T*
(across all servers.) Tj
T*
(Mathematical Derivation:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Mesh Topology Calculations \(N = 16\):) Tj
T*
(- Dedicated physical links = N x \(N - 1\) / 2 = 16 x 15 / 2 = 120 duplex cables.) Tj
T*
(- I/O ports per server = N - 1 = 15 ports per server.) Tj
T*
(- Total network I/O ports = 16 servers x 15 ports = 240 ports.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Star Topology Calculations \(N = 16 with central switch\):) Tj
T*
(- Dedicated physical links = N = 16 cables.) Tj
T*
(- I/O ports per server = 1 port per server \(Total = 16 server ports + 16 switch ports =) Tj
T*
(32 ports\).) Tj
T*
(* 3. Architectural Conclusion: Mesh topology requires 7.5x more physical cabling \(120) Tj
T*
(vs 16\) and 7.5x more server ports \(240 vs 32\), illustrating why Star topology) Tj
T*
(dominates standard LAN architectures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([PROBLEM 2: Data Link Layer Cyclic Redundancy Check \(CRC\) Derivation]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Statement: A data link layer sender transmits a 10-bit data frame D =) Tj
T*
(1010010011. The generator divisor polynomial is G = 10011 \(degree r = 4\). Calculate the) Tj
T*
(4-bit CRC remainder \(checksum\) appended to the transmitted frame, and demonstrate) Tj
T*
(receiver-side verification.) Tj
T*
(Step-by-Step Modulo-2 Arithmetic Execution:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Append r = 4 zeros to data frame D: Dividend = 1010010011 0000 \(14 bits\).) Tj
T*
(* 2. Modulo-2 Binary Division \(XOR operations without borrow\):) Tj
T*
(- Divide 10100100110000 by 10011:) Tj
T*
(- Step 1: 10100 XOR 10011 = 00111 -> Bring down 1 -> 01111.) Tj
T*
(- Step 2: Next bit 0 -> bring down 0 -> 11110 XOR 10011 = 01101.) Tj
T*
(- Step 3: Bring down 0 -> 11010 XOR 10011 = 01001.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
