([PROBLEM 3: End-to-End OSI Protocol Encapsulation Walkthrough]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Statement: Trace the step-by-step encapsulation process when a user clicks a) Tj
T*
(link in a web browser to download a webpage from a remote web server.) Tj
T*
(Protocol Flow & Header Attachment Trace:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Application Layer: Browser generates HTTP GET request. Payload = "GET) Tj
T*
(/index.html HTTP/1.1".) Tj
T*
(* 2. Transport Layer: Encapsulates HTTP payload inside a TCP Segment by adding TCP) Tj
T*
(Header \(Source Port = 54321, Destination Port = 80/443, Sequence Number = 1001,) Tj
T*
(Window Size, Checksum\).) Tj
T*
(* 3. Network Layer: Encapsulates TCP segment inside an IP Packet by adding IP Header) Tj
T*
(\(Source IP = 192.168.1.50, Destination IP = 93.184.216.34, TTL = 64, Protocol = 6 for) Tj
T*
(TCP\).) Tj
T*
(* 4. Data Link Layer: Encapsulates IP packet inside an Ethernet Frame by adding) Tj
T*
(Ethernet Header \(Source MAC = 3C:52:82:11:22:33, Gateway Router MAC =) Tj
T*
(00:1A:2B:3C:4D:5E, EtherType = 0x0800\) and Ethernet Trailer \(4-byte CRC/FCS\).) Tj
T*
(* 5. Physical Layer: Transduces Ethernet frame bits into Manchester electrical pulses) Tj
T*
(/ optical photons onto the physical transmission line.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([PROBLEM 4: Bandwidth-Delay Product & Transmission Delay Analysis]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Statement: A 100 Mbps fiber optic communication link spans a transcontinental) Tj
T*
(distance of 4000 km. Signal propagation speed in fiber is 2 x 10^8 m/s. Calculate: \(1\)) Tj
T*
(Propagation Delay \(t_prop\), \(2\) Transmission Delay \(t_trans\) for a 2.5 MB file, and \(3\)) Tj
T*
(Bandwidth-Delay Product \(BDP\) in bits and bytes.) Tj
T*
(Mathematical Derivation:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Propagation Delay: t_prop = Distance / Speed = \(4000 x 10^3 m\) / \(2 x 10^8 m/s\)) Tj
T*
(= 0.02 seconds = 20 milliseconds \(ms\).) Tj
T*
(* 2. Transmission Delay: File size = 2.5 MB = 2.5 x 10^6 x 8 bits = 20,000,000 bits.) Tj
T*
(Bandwidth = 100 Mbps = 100 x 10^6 bps. t_trans = Size / Bandwidth = 20 x 10^6 / 100 x) Tj
T*
(10^6 = 0.20 seconds = 200 ms.) Tj
T*
ET

