(* 3. Bandwidth-Delay Product \(BDP\):) Tj
T*
(- BDP represents the total volume of data bits that can be "in flight" on the) Tj
T*
(transmission wire simultaneously.) Tj
T*
(- BDP = Bandwidth x Propagation Delay = \(100 x 10^6 bps\) x 0.02 s = 2,000,000 bits =) Tj
T*
(250,000 Bytes = 250 KB.) Tj
T*
(* 4. Engineering Impact: To achieve 100% link utilization, the TCP sliding window) Tj
T*
(size must be configured to at least 250 KB.) Tj
T*
